From: lutvzn <106083845+lutvzn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:15:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] qualcommax: ipq50xx: redmi-ax3000: lower the free memory
 floor to 8 MiB

With the NSS region and the Q6 firmware regions reserved, Linux gets
~173 MiB of the board's 256 MiB. /etc/init.d/sysctl sets
vm.min_free_kbytes=16384 on every board above 64 MiB, so the kernel keeps
20-24 MiB idle (low/high watermarks) and MemAvailable stays around
25 MiB with both radios and the NSS plane up.

Write /etc/sysctl.d/20-min-free.conf with 8192, the value the same
script uses on 64 MiB boards, on first boot. It is applied after the
default and stays editable.

Measured with the value set at runtime: MemAvailable 25 -> 44-48 MiB;
twelve 20 s iperf3 runs and a 30 min bidirectional run (4 streams each
way, Wi-Fi <-> LAN through the NSS plane, ~610 Mbit/s combined) showed
no page allocation failures and unchanged throughput.
---
 .../etc/uci-defaults/15_min_free_kbytes       | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/uci-defaults/15_min_free_kbytes

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/uci-defaults/15_min_free_kbytes b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/uci-defaults/15_min_free_kbytes
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..96a19658d0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/uci-defaults/15_min_free_kbytes
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+conf=/etc/sysctl.d/20-min-free.conf
+[ -e "$conf" ] && exit 0
+
+case "$(board_name)" in
+xiaomi,redmi-ax3000)
+	# 256 MiB, of which the NSS and Q6 reservations leave ~173 MiB to
+	# Linux. /etc/init.d/sysctl keeps 16 MiB free on every board above
+	# 64 MiB (watermarks 16/20/24 MiB); 8 MiB is its value for 64 MiB
+	# boards and held up under NSS and Wi-Fi offload load.
+	cat > "$conf" <<EOF
+# Free memory floor for this board, applied after /etc/init.d/sysctl's
+# default. Raise it again if "page allocation failure" shows in dmesg.
+vm.min_free_kbytes=8192
+EOF
+	;;
+esac
+
+exit 0
